cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use nmr_bind_fit in your research, please cite the software repository and the archived release used for your analysis."
title: "nmr_bind_fit: transparent model comparison and uncertainty reporting for NMR host-guest titrations"
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21071370
authors:
  - family-names: Sohn
    given-names: Dae Hyup
repository-code: "https://github.com/dhsohn/nmr_bind_fit"
url: "https://github.com/dhsohn/nmr_bind_fit"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - NMR
  - host-guest chemistry
  - supramolecular chemistry
  - binding titration
  - model comparison
  - bootstrap
abstract: >-
  nmr_bind_fit is a Python command-line workflow for NMR chemical-shift
  titration binding analysis. It fits 1:1, sequential 1:2, sequential 2:1,
  and non-binding candidate models, reports information-criterion model
  comparisons and bootstrap uncertainty, and generates reproducible analysis
  summaries for host-guest binding studies.
